{%- comment -%}
  The file table: files directly in the directory, then its subdirectories.
  Included by subgraph.liquid; reads `files`, `subdirs` and `summary`.

  A subdirectory row says WHAT IT IS when the caller resolved a description
  for it, and falls back to a file count when nothing declares one. The
  description is preferred because a count drifts on every commit that adds a
  file: one line of `beans/README.md` conflicted three times in a single day
  (2026-10-01), each branch computing a different total from the same
  generator and none of them right for the merge.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if summary != "" -%}
_{{ summary }}_

{% endif -%}
{%- if files.size == 0 and subdirs.size == 0 and summary == "" -%}
_This directory holds no files yet._
{%- else -%}
| file | what it is | used by |
|---|---|---|
{% for f in files -%}
| [`{{ f.path }}`]({{ f.href }}) | {{ f.what }} | {{ f.usedBy }} |
{% endfor -%}
{% for d in subdirs -%}
| [`{{ d.name }}/`]({% if d.readme != "" %}{{ d.readme }}{% else %}{{ d.href }}/{% endif %}) | {% if d.description != "" %}{{ d.description }}{% else %}{{ d.count }} file{% if d.count != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% endif %} | |
{% endfor -%}
{%- endif %}
